course: dictionary
lesson: 6383
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. «Let me mull it over» means think carefully for some time, not something to drink.
explain: «Now we shall be able to mull some ale!» Ale is a drink, so to mull it means to heat it with spices. Always try your meaning in the sentence and check that it makes sense.
explain: Mull can also be a place name with a capital letter: Mull is a large island off the west coast of Scotland. When you see a capital letter, ask whether it is a name.
fact: «Mull» means to think about something carefully for some time.
fact: «Mulled» wine, cider or juice is heated with sugar and spices, often in winter.
fact: Mull is a large island off the west coast of Scotland.
fact: «Mull» is also a Scottish word for a headland, which is a high piece of land running into the sea.
exercise: «Let me mull it over before I choose.» What does mull mean here? | To count the money | To laugh loudly | *To think about something carefully for some time | To heat something with spices
exercise: The Rat says, «Now we shall be able to mull some ale!» What is being mulled? | The cheese on the table | A bag of seeds | *Ale, a drink that is heated with spices | A cold stone
exercise: Which of these is Mull? | A desert in Africa | A town in the middle of England | A river in Wales | *A large island off the west coast of Scotland
test: Mum says, «Mulled apple juice is warm and spicy at Christmas.» What does mulled mean? | Squeezed very hard | *Heated with sugar and spices | Cooled down with ice | Poured into a glass
test: Ravi says, «I need to mull over my answer.» What does Ravi need? | To eat quickly | *Time to think carefully | To read a map | To go outside
exam: Which sentence uses mull to mean heat with spices? | «The island of Mull is far away.» | *«We could mull some cider for the party.» | «I will mull over the sum.» | «She had to mull the plan again.»
